{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"gh api repos/mrkkucharski/vgt/issues/8/comments --jq '.[] | {user:.user.login,body}' && gh api repos/mrkkucharski/vgt/issues/9/comments --jq '.[] | {user:.user.login,body}'\"","aggregated_output":"{\"body\":\"Checked the declared dependency before implementation: #7 (analysis foundation + schema v2) remains open with `status:needs-fix`, and this branch does not contain its sidecar/stage interface. I have not duplicated or cherry-picked its unreviewed implementation into #8; this issue can proceed once #7 is accepted/merged or the orchestrator provides its accepted foundation.\",\"user\":\"mrkkucharski\"}\n{\"body\":\"Implemented the tempo/beat/downbeat stage on top of #7's analysis foundation.\\n\\nNote on dependency ordering: #7 (\\\"Sub 1\\\") is still open (`status:needs-fix`, not a native GitHub sub-issue of #8), so this branch merges in `issue-7-phase-1-analysis-foundation-vgt-sidecar` directly to get the `.vgt` schema v2 / stage-cache framework this issue builds on. Once #7 lands on `main`, this branch should rebase cleanly (no conflicts expected — #7's commits are already included verbatim via the merge).\\n\\n## What's implemented\\n- `src/vgt/tempo.py`: `detect_beats` (madmom DBN beat+downbeat primary, librosa `beat_track` fallback) and `build_tempo_grid` (least-squares constant-BPM fit vs. piecewise-linear spans, decided by the global fit's relative residual — see the tempo-map rule in `docs/GOAL.md`). Also renders the click-over-mix verification artifact.\\n- `madmom` is isolated behind an optional `madmom` extra (`pyproject.toml`), confirmed fragile exactly as the issue warned: madmom 0.16.1 (its last release) doesn't even import on Python 3.11 (`collections.MutableSequence` was removed in 3.10, `pkg_resources` needs `setuptools\\u003c81`). The librosa fallback is therefore the practical default path and ships unconditionally.\\n- Wired into `vgt analyze`'s `tempo` stage; output includes `bpm`, `downbeat_offset_seconds`, `time_signature`, `mode` (`constant`/`piecewise`), `residual_seconds`, `spans` (when piecewise), `backend`, and `click_artifact_path`.\\n\\n## Verified against the fixture\\n- `vgt analyze` on `test/Reaper Project` detects a clean constant 120.0 BPM grid via the librosa fallback in ~2s and writes `Reaper Project.vgt-tempo-click.wav` next to the sidecar (gitignored — it's a regenerated verification artifact, not source).\\n- Manual tempo correction (`human_verified: true`) persists across re-runs (existing generic stage-cache test, now exercised against the real detector).\\n- `uv run pytest`: 17 passed.\\n\\n## Acceptance criteria\\n- [x] Beat grid (bpm, downbeat offset, time signature, mode, residual) written to the sidecar for the fixture.\\n- [x] Click-over-mix artifact generated (audibly locks — verified by inspecting duration/channels/sample rate; I can't audition it myself, but the render pipeline is straightforward `librosa.clicks` mixed over the loaded source).\\n- [x] A tempo/downbeat correction persists across re-runs.\",\"user\":\"mrkkucharski\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
